<h2>Segment 230 &mdash; the world and conceptions</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s230S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w1">rigs pa <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s230m2">drug cu</span> pa</span> las <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p3">kyang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w4">&#x27;jig rten</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w5">ma rig</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w6">rkyen</span> <span class="u gram" data-d="6" data-l="s230p7">can</span> du, , <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w8">gang phyir</span> rdzogs pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w9">sangs rgyas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w10">gsungs</span>, , <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w11">de yi phyir na</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w12">&#x27;jig rten</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w13">&#x27;di</span>, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w14">rnam rtog</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p15">yin</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p16">zhes</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p17">cis</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w18">mi &#x27;thad</span>, , ces gsungs pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w19">don</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w20">&#x27;grel par</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w21">&#x27;jig rten</span> <span class="u gram" data-d="6" data-l="s230p22">rnams</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w23">rang</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p24">gi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w25">ngo bos</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p26">ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w27">grub pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w28">rtog pas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w29">btags pa</span> tsam du bshad cing</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s230S">The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w1"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s230m2">Sixty</span> Verses on Reasoning</span> say <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p3">as well</span>, The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w4">world</span> is something that <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w5">ignorance</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w6">causes</span>; Why? <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w8">For</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w9">Buddhas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w10">say</span> it is so. And <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p17">why</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w11">then</span> would it be <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w18">wrong</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p16">to say</span> That <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w13">this</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w12">world</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p15">is</span> only <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w14">conceptions</span>. The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w19">meaning</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p24">of</span> this verse, according to the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w20">commentary</span>, is that <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p26">none</span> of the many <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w21">worlds</span> that exist <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230w27">does so</span> through some <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w25">essence</span> of its <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w23">own</span>: none of them are anything more than <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w29">products</span> of our <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w28">conception</span>.<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p7"><span class="nul">Possession of a cause is recast in the English causal verb causes; no separate exponent of can.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s230p22"><span class="nul">Plural force is fused into worlds; the extra many is not claimed.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Provisional machine alignment by Codex, independent Tibetan-first proposal. Sixty Verses on Reasoning is a work title, with its literal numeral member. ma rig is the established ignorance compound, not separately negated. rkyen is recast as the causal verb causes; can has no separate exponent in that conversion. gang phyir supplies causal For; the separate Why? is a rhetorical recast and is left unwrapped. mi 'thad is a negative phrase matched whole to wrong, not 'thad alone. The commentary's existence predicate grub pa is the English anaphoric does so, kept at phrase depth. rang/gi/ngo bos target essence of its own in English order; instrumental force lies outside the selected essence word. rnams is null only for plural morphology fused into worlds. tsam is omitted because restriction is distributed over none of them are anything more than, not cleanly isolated. rdzogs pa'i and quotation/description scaffolding without secure separate exponents are omitted. C05:235 repeats the quoted verse; C16:807 changes conceptions to projections, and ILL:1106 supplies a differently worded English rendering. These comparisons do not establish publication or ingestion independence.</div>
